/*
    These inline functions locate the table interval for an input value and
    return whether the value lies inside the stored polynomial support.
    lower:    lower boundary of the first table;
    upper:    upper boundary of the first table and lower boundary of the
              second table;
    max:      upper boundary of the second table;
    stride0:  stride of the first table;
    stride1:  stride of the second table;
    xx:       input value, replaced by its local coordinate in the selected
              interval;
    table_idx:  location of the table data for the selected interval.

    Outside the stored support, `xx` is replaced by the local coordinate of
    the nearest support endpoint and `in_domain` is false.  The callers then
    continue the endpoint polynomial with its stored first derivative, which
    keeps the tabulated value and its sensitivity mutually consistent while
    avoiding extrapolation with an unsupported high-order polynomial.
*/

